<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Sarcoma</journal-id><journal-title>Sarcoma</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1357-714X</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1369-1643</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">18521316</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2395459</article-id>            <article-id pub-id-type="pii">S1357714X01000299</article-id>            <article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/13577140120099209</article-id>      <article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Surgical Treatment of Chondrosarcoma of the Sternum</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>            <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Ashford</surname><given-names>Robert U.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>            <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Stanton</surname><given-names>Jeremy</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff2">2</xref></contrib>            <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Khan</surname><given-names>Farid</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff3">3</xref></contrib>            <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Pringle</surname><given-names>Jean A. S.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff4">4</xref></contrib>            <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Cannon</surname><given-names>Stephen R.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff4">4</xref></contrib>            <contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Briggs</surname><given-names>Timothy W. R.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff4">4</xref></contrib>      </contrib-group>            <aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>                <addr-line>Hull Royal Infirmary</addr-line>                <addr-line>Hull</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff2"><label>2</label>                <addr-line>Colchester General Hospital</addr-line>                <addr-line>Colchester</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff3"><label>3</label>                <addr-line>Queen Elizabeth Hospital</addr-line>                <addr-line>Woolwich</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff4"><label>4</label>                <addr-line>The London Bone and Soft Tissue Tumour Service</addr-line>                <addr-line>The Royal National Orthopaedic Hospital</addr-line>                <addr-line>Brockley Hill, Stanmore</addr-line>                <addr-line>Middlesex</addr-line>                <addr-line>MA7 4LP</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>        <pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>12</month><year>2001</year></pub-date><volume>5</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>209</fpage><lpage>213</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2001 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2001</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>            <p><italic>Purpose:</italic> We reviewed all tumours of the sternum referred to The London Bone and Soft Tissue Tumour Service between1956 and 1997 inclusive.</p><p><italic>Patients and results:</italic> There were eight patients with this pathology, the male to female ratio was 3:1 and their mean age was53 years. Of these patients, three are alive and disease free, one is alive with recurrence, and four have died, two of the consequencesof the disease and two of unrelated causes. Surgery is the principal treatment of these tumours both for excision andsubsequent reconstruction.</p><p><italic>Discussion:</italic> Extended disease-free survival is possible with correct diagnosis, complete excision at the first operation, appropriateskeletal reconstruction, adequate skin cover and appropriate postoperative support and follow-up.</p>        </abstract></article-meta></front></article>